From c783d99fe0e609eab96e0dfda441d40873378ed5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:37:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(launch): bound the launcher preflight; a slow PM check no
 longer holds commands hostage [daveey]

prepare_launch asked PM whether the venv was current with no deadline (worker
start, runtime validation, response), and check_runtime repeated the
plugin-union/YAML work on every dispatch. On a loaded Mac mini that made short
`hermes kanban` calls exceed 60 s. A current launch also republished launchers
(importing app config) whenever the launching interpreter path differed.

- hermes_cli/launch_probe.py: passive currency/runtime probe in an isolated
  worker with one monotonic 1 s deadline; its process group is SIGKILLed on
  every exit. No answer = unknown, never current or stale.
- prepare_launch: unknown skips repair and publication and leaves completion
  debt (and says so on stderr when an update is still owed), but still hands
  off once to the managed (signed) interpreter. The verdict (current/unknown)
  rides a same-pid one-shot env handoff (venv_sync.exec_launch) so the exec'd
  child neither re-probes nor waits out a second deadline; it is withdrawn if
  the exec fails.
- `hermes update` (not its report-only forms) keeps the full, unbounded check:
  it is the remedy every deferred launch names.
- A current launch publishes only when a checkout launcher is missing, dead
  or pinned to a stale same-store Python (mirrors ensure_install_launchers).
- check_runtime reuses this launch's current/unknown verdict, is bounded the
  same way, and honors HERMES_DISABLE_LAZY_INSTALLS.
- Windows keeps the previous (unbounded) path: no native containment yet.

Tests: test_launch_preflight_bound blocks real PM client dispatch (at runtime
preparation and at the response) both in-process and in the probe worker, and
blocks pm.activate in the runtime diagnostic: prepare_launch and check_runtime
each return within the probe budget, debt kept, nothing published/synced,
blocked descendants gone. RED on base: both cases hang until the 60 s outer
timeout. Also a real execv handoff (same pid, verdict received), failed-exec
withdrawal, the owed-update notice, and update's unbounded path.
